🤖🎵
The control row is hard to see because the chrome buttons are painted as a slightly darker hole in the quiz panel, with a hairline that never reaches the 3:1 non-text floor. The rest of the quiz is in good shape; this is tweak-mode, not a redesign.

Live brand data was fetched (`https://www.liatrio.ai/brand-data.json`, `lastUpdated: 2026-04-14`). No palette conflict with the local design system.

## Brand Audit

- **Scope:** Quiz section in the explainer shell (`section.quiz`): eyebrow, instructions, `.quiz-control-row`, progress/score, answer list, feedback. Template CSS in `skills/interactive-explainer-html/references/explainer-template.html`.
- **Compliant:** Dark-first canvas `#1A1F23` / elevated panel `#1E2327`. Space Grotesk. Sentence-case chrome labels (`Reset questions`, `Previous question`). Uppercase tracked eyebrow. Bright Green used as signal (progress fill, selected border, focus ring `2px` / `2px` offset). Hot Red only on incorrect. Focus-visible is already the brand recipe. Layout and one-question flow should stay.
- **Issues:** Chrome and answer options share one `button` rule, so toolbar chrome and choice cards cannot follow different recipes. Button fill `#1A1F23` on `#1E2327` is **1.05:1**. Hairline `#2A3036` on the panel is **1.19:1**. Both fail WCAG 1.4.11 (3:1 for non-text UI). Radius is `8px` (`--r-2`); in-app chrome should be **6px**, choice cards **12px**. Labels are weight 400; buttons should be **500**. Hover only recolors the border; brand hover also lightens a dark surface ~6%. Empty progress track uses the same 1.19:1 hairline, so an unanswered bar almost disappears. Unselected answers have the same ghost-border problem until selected.
- **Fixes:** Split chrome buttons from answer buttons. Keep the four-button split and copy. Restyle chrome to the nav/in-app recipe with a graphite outline strong enough to hit 3:1. Treat answers as selectable cards. Nudge the progress track. Do not fill all four chrome buttons Bright Green — that would steal the one accent from selection, progress, and focus.
- **Verification:** Contrast math against `#1E2327`: white 15.85:1, `#CCCCCC` 9.87:1, `#89DF00` 9.52:1, `#24AE1D` 5.39:1, `#E63946` border 3.80:1, disabled label at 0.55 opacity still ~5.8:1. Failures are the control *edges*, not the type.
- **Source Validation:** `references/liatrio-design-system.md`, `references/liatrio-component-recipes.md`, `assets/colors_and_type.css`, live `brand-data.json` checked.

## Suggested chrome-button update

These are product chrome, not marketing CTAs, so use the **6px in-app** language, not square filled greens.

Keep left Reset/Randomize and right Previous/Next. Change only paint and type:

```css
.quiz-actions button,
.quiz-nav-actions button {
  border: 1px solid var(--fg-subtle); /* #999999 → 5.56:1 on the panel */
  border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 8px 16px;
  background: #2C3034; /* ~6% lift off #1E2327 */
  color: var(--ink);
  font-weight: 500;
  text-align: center;
}

.quiz-actions button:hover:not(:disabled),
.quiz-nav-actions button:hover:not(:disabled) {
  border-color: var(--bright-green);
  background: #32373B;
}

.quiz-nav-actions button:disabled {
  opacity: 1;
  color: var(--fg-subtle);
  border-color: #666666; /* ~2.8:1; still a visible control, not a hole */
  background: var(--dark-bg-2);
}
```

`--fg-subtle` is Grey 400 from the brand ramp. `--border-strong` (`#3A4046`) is only **1.51:1** here, so it would not fix the original problem.

Optional one-step hierarchy, still the same interaction: when **Next** is enabled, use the outlined-secondary recipe (`background: rgba(137, 223, 0, 0.10); color: #89DF00; border-color: #89DF00`). Leave Reset, Randomize, and Previous graphite.

## Other quiz tweaks worth doing in the same pass

1. **Answer options as cards, not the same `button` rule.** `border-radius: 12px`, unselected border `#666666` or `#999999`, keep Bright Green selected border, add the card inset glow `box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgba(137, 223, 0, 0.18) inset` on the chosen answer. Wrong stays Hot Red border-only.
2. **Progress track.** Paint the empty track `#666666` or `#3A4046` at minimum so “0 of 8” still shows a bar. Keep the Bright Green fill and the current thickness.
3. **Hover/press.** 120ms, dark fill lightens ~6%, `scale(0.98)` on press. Focus ring can stay as-is.
4. **Question heading weight 600**, chrome labels 500. Do not uppercase the four buttons.

Leave alone in tweak mode: one-question paging, Reset/Randomize shuffle, score as `N of M correct`, Bright Green as the section’s only accent, quiz motion timing, feedback copy and left-rail treatment.

I would apply (1) chrome split + Grey 400 outline, (2) answer cards, and (3) a slightly stronger progress track in the **template**, then rebuild this Herdr file from it. Say if you want the optional green **Next**, or if graphite chrome on all four is the right call.

